"The postoperative pathology demonstrated a Gleason 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2) and pathological T2 stage with no extraprostatic extension. Reassuring findings include negative surgical margins, no invasion of the seminal vesicles, and absence of lymphovascular invasion. However, nodal status is uncertain as no nodes were removed, meaning pNx does not establish node-negative disease. The preoperative PSA level was 5.3. The documented surgical findings are favorable regarding local disease control. The primary uncertainty in prognosis stems from the missing postoperative PSA and its subsequent trajectory, which is necessary to assess biochemical recurrence. Missing nodal sampling further widens the uncertainty regarding regional disease control. Information regarding postoperative PSA and its trajectory would be crucial in revising the prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 73.10 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 47.51–98.68 months; its coverage has not been validated."
